  "title": "Mozarabic Ordo missae core, 1804 (Dominica prima de adventu): complete constituent",
  "extent_kind": "constituent",
  "excluded_book_divisions": [
    "All other Missal divisions and appendices",
    "Preceding parts of the Order of Mass and of Dominica prima de adventu, from the Officium through the Inlatio, Sanctus and Post Sanctus",
    "Following parts of the Order of Mass from the commixtion rubric Sic faciat presbiter onward",
    "Printed column and marginal line numbers, running heads and the signature Miss.Moz. B"
  ],
  "scope": "The fixed core of the Mozarabic Mass order as printed within Dominica prima de adventu, together with the two variable Advent I prayers printed inside that span, printed cols. 12-17: from the rubric Deinde dicat Presb. in silentio before Adesto, through the institution narrative, the Advent I post pridie, Te praestante, Dominus sit semper vobiscum and Fidem, the creed, the fraction rubric and numbered figure, the Advent I prayer ad orationem dominicam, the Pater noster with its responses and the Liberati embolism through its Amen. The marginal Forma ista note and the Roman consecration form printed below the columns are included. All other matter on these pages is excluded.",
